# EtAccordion Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtAccordion` is a collapsible accordion component for the eToro design system. It provides a flexible, accessible accordion with:

- **Compound component pattern**: `EtAccordion.Item`, `EtAccordion.Header`, and `EtAccordion.Content` subcomponents
- **Expand/collapse states**: single or multiple items can be expanded simultaneously
- **Built-in animations**: smooth height animation for content, rotating chevron icon
- **Controlled & uncontrolled modes**: supports both state management approaches
- **Context-based state sharing**: expansion state shared via React Context to subcomponents
- **Accessibility support**: proper ARIA roles and states for screen readers

**Does NOT handle:**

- Custom expand/collapse icons (chevron only, can be hidden)
- Nested accordions (single level only)
- Drag-to-reorder functionality

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtAccordion` (main component)

```tsx
<EtAccordion
  allowMultiple?: boolean         // default: false
  defaultExpandedIds?: string[]   // default: []
  expandedIds?: string[]          // controlled mode
  onExpandedChange?: (ids: string[]) => void
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
>
  {children}
</EtAccordion>
```

**Children constraints:**

- Must contain one or more `EtAccordion.Item` components
- Each item must have a unique `id` prop
- No other components should be direct children

**State management:**

- **Uncontrolled**: Use `defaultExpandedIds` for initial state, component manages state internally
- **Controlled**: Use `expandedIds` + `onExpandedChange` to manage state externally
- When `allowMultiple` is `false` (default), only one item can be expanded at a time

### `EtAccordion.Item`

```tsx
<EtAccordion.Item
  id: string                      // required - unique identifier
  disabled?: boolean              // default: false
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
>
  {children}
</EtAccordion.Item>
```

**Children constraints:**

- Should contain exactly one `EtAccordion.Header` and one `EtAccordion.Content`
- Order doesn't matter (Header should typically come before Content for logical layout)

**Behavior:**

- Provides item-specific context (`id`, `isExpanded`, `disabled`, `toggle`) to children
- Renders a divider below each item
- When `disabled`, header is not clickable and shows reduced opacity

### `EtAccordion.Header`

```tsx
<EtAccordion.Header
  showChevron?: boolean           // default: true
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
>
  <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">Question text</EtText>
</EtAccordion.Header>
```

**Children constraints:**

- **Must be EtText component(s) only** - throws runtime error if other components or raw text are passed
- This ensures consistent typography and styling across all accordions
- Recommended variant for questions: `body-base-semibold`
- **Color override**: Any color passed via EtText `style` is overridden by the header's `textPrimaryNeutral` (Figma overlay-neutral-text)

**Behavior:**

- Clickable area that toggles the parent item's expanded state
- Applies `textPrimaryNeutral` color to EtText children (Figma overlay-neutral-text)
- Contains an animated chevron icon that rotates 180° when expanded
- Receives expansion state via `AccordionItemContext` (no prop drilling needed)
- Applies pressed opacity feedback on touch
- Supports accessibility with `accessibilityRole="button"` and `accessibilityState`

### `EtAccordion.Content`

```tsx
<EtAccordion.Content
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
  testID?: string
>
  <EtText variant="body-base-regular">Answer text</EtText>
</EtAccordion.Content>
```

**Children constraints:**

- **Must be EtText component(s) only** - throws runtime error if other components or raw text are passed
- This ensures consistent typography and styling across all accordions
- Recommended variant for answers: `body-base-regular`

**Behavior:**

- Animated container that smoothly expands/collapses
- Height animation duration: 300ms
- Uses absolute positioning internally to ensure proper layout during animation
- Receives expansion state via `AccordionItemContext`
- Hidden when collapsed (height: 0, overflow: hidden)

## Usage Patterns

### Basic accordion (single expansion)

```tsx
<EtAccordion>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="1">
    <EtAccordion.Header>
      <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">What is copy trading?</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Header>
    <EtAccordion.Content>
      <EtText variant="body-base-regular">Copy trading allows you to automatically copy the trades of experienced investors.</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Content>
  </EtAccordion.Item>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="2">
    <EtAccordion.Header>
      <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">How do I get started?</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Header>
    <EtAccordion.Content>
      <EtText variant="body-base-regular">Sign up for an account and complete the verification process.</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Content>
  </EtAccordion.Item>
</EtAccordion>
```

### Multiple items expanded

```tsx
<EtAccordion allowMultiple defaultExpandedIds={['1', '2']}>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="1">
    <EtAccordion.Header>
      <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">Section 1</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Header>
    <EtAccordion.Content>
      <EtText variant="body-base-regular">Content 1</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Content>
  </EtAccordion.Item>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="2">
    <EtAccordion.Header>
      <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">Section 2</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Header>
    <EtAccordion.Content>
      <EtText variant="body-base-regular">Content 2</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Content>
  </EtAccordion.Item>
</EtAccordion>
```

### Controlled accordion

```tsx
const [expandedIds, setExpandedIds] = useState<string[]>(['1']);

<EtAccordion expandedIds={expandedIds} onExpandedChange={setExpandedIds}>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="1">
    <EtAccordion.Header>
      <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">Question 1?</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Header>
    <EtAccordion.Content>
      <EtText variant="body-base-regular">Answer 1</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Content>
  </EtAccordion.Item>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="2">
    <EtAccordion.Header>
      <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">Question 2?</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Header>
    <EtAccordion.Content>
      <EtText variant="body-base-regular">Answer 2</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Content>
  </EtAccordion.Item>
</EtAccordion>;
```

### Disabled item

```tsx
<EtAccordion>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="1">
    <EtAccordion.Header>
      <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">Active Section</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Header>
    <EtAccordion.Content>
      <EtText variant="body-base-regular">This can be expanded.</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Content>
  </EtAccordion.Item>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="2" disabled>
    <EtAccordion.Header>
      <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">Disabled Section</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Header>
    <EtAccordion.Content>
      <EtText variant="body-base-regular">This cannot be expanded.</EtText>
    </EtAccordion.Content>
  </EtAccordion.Item>
</EtAccordion>
```

### Header without chevron

```tsx
<EtAccordion.Item id="1">
  <EtAccordion.Header showChevron={false}>
    <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">Custom Header</EtText>
  </EtAccordion.Header>
  <EtAccordion.Content>
    <EtText variant="body-base-regular">Content here</EtText>
  </EtAccordion.Content>
</EtAccordion.Item>
```

### Dynamic items from data

```tsx
const faqItems = [
  { id: '1', question: 'What is eToro?', answer: 'eToro is a social trading platform.' },
  { id: '2', question: 'Is it safe?', answer: 'Yes, eToro is regulated by multiple authorities.' },
];

<EtAccordion>
  {faqItems.map((item) => (
    <EtAccordion.Item key={item.id} id={item.id}>
      <EtAccordion.Header>
        <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">{item.question}</EtText>
      </EtAccordion.Header>
      <EtAccordion.Content>
        <EtText variant="body-base-regular">{item.answer}</EtText>
      </EtAccordion.Content>
    </EtAccordion.Item>
  ))}
</EtAccordion>;
```

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using non-EtText children in Header or Content

```tsx
// BAD - raw string text will throw error
<EtAccordion.Header>Question text</EtAccordion.Header>

// BAD - View/other components will throw error
<EtAccordion.Header>
  <View><Text>Question</Text></View>
</EtAccordion.Header>

// BAD - React Native Text will throw error
<EtAccordion.Content>
  <Text>Answer text</Text>
</EtAccordion.Content>
```

**Fix:** Always wrap content in EtText components:

```tsx
<EtAccordion.Header>
  <EtText variant="body-base-semibold">Question text</EtText>
</EtAccordion.Header>

<EtAccordion.Content>
  <EtText variant="body-base-regular">Answer text</EtText>
</EtAccordion.Content>
```

### ❌ Missing item id

```tsx
// BAD - id is required for each item
<EtAccordion.Item>
  <EtAccordion.Header>Header</EtAccordion.Header>
  <EtAccordion.Content>Content</EtAccordion.Content>
</EtAccordion.Item>
```

**Fix:** Always provide a unique `id` prop:

```tsx
<EtAccordion.Item id="unique-id">
  <EtAccordion.Header>Header</EtAccordion.Header>
  <EtAccordion.Content>Content</EtAccordion.Content>
</EtAccordion.Item>
```

### ❌ Using subcomponents outside of EtAccordion

```tsx
// BAD - will throw runtime error
<EtAccordion.Header>Header</EtAccordion.Header>

// BAD - will throw runtime error
<EtAccordion.Content>Content</EtAccordion.Content>

// BAD - will throw runtime error
<EtAccordion.Item id="1">...</EtAccordion.Item>
```

**Fix:** Always wrap subcomponents inside their parent components:

```tsx
<EtAccordion>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="1">
    <EtAccordion.Header>Header</EtAccordion.Header>
    <EtAccordion.Content>Content</EtAccordion.Content>
  </EtAccordion.Item>
</EtAccordion>
```

### ❌ Duplicate item IDs

```tsx
// BAD - duplicate IDs will cause unexpected behavior
<EtAccordion>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="1">...</EtAccordion.Item>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="1">...</EtAccordion.Item>
</EtAccordion>
```

**Fix:** Ensure each item has a unique ID:

```tsx
<EtAccordion>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="1">...</EtAccordion.Item>
  <EtAccordion.Item id="2">...</EtAccordion.Item>
</EtAccordion>
```

### ❌ Mixing controlled and uncontrolled props

```tsx
// BAD - don't use defaultExpandedIds with expandedIds
<EtAccordion defaultExpandedIds={['1']} expandedIds={expandedIds} onExpandedChange={setExpandedIds}>
  ...
</EtAccordion>
```

**Fix:** Use either controlled or uncontrolled mode, not both:

```tsx
// Controlled
<EtAccordion expandedIds={expandedIds} onExpandedChange={setExpandedIds}>
  ...
</EtAccordion>

// OR Uncontrolled
<EtAccordion defaultExpandedIds={['1']}>
  ...
</EtAccordion>
```

### ❌ Manually managing expansion state incorrectly

```tsx
// BAD - onExpandedChange provides the new state array, don't compute it again
<EtAccordion
  expandedIds={expandedIds}
  onExpandedChange={(ids) => {
    // Wrong! The ids parameter already has the correct new state
    if (ids.includes(currentId)) {
      setExpandedIds(ids.filter((id) => id !== currentId));
    } else {
      setExpandedIds([...ids, currentId]);
    }
  }}
>
  ...
</EtAccordion>
```

**Fix:** `onExpandedChange` receives the complete new state:

```tsx
<EtAccordion expandedIds={expandedIds} onExpandedChange={(ids) => setExpandedIds(ids)}>
  ...
</EtAccordion>
```

### ❌ Expecting multiple expansion without allowMultiple

```tsx
// BAD - without allowMultiple, only one item can be expanded
<EtAccordion defaultExpandedIds={['1', '2', '3']}>...</EtAccordion>
```

**Fix:** Enable `allowMultiple` for multiple expanded items:

```tsx
<EtAccordion allowMultiple defaultExpandedIds={['1', '2', '3']}>
  ...
</EtAccordion>
```

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - provides theme colors for styling (divider, chevron colors)
- `EtoroIcon` - underlying icon component for chevron in `EtAccordion.Header`
- `AccordionContext` - React context for sharing expanded state with items
- `AccordionItemContext` - React context for sharing item-specific state with Header/Content
- `useAccordionState` - hook managing expanded state (controlled/uncontrolled)
- `useAccordionAnimation` - hook managing chevron rotation animation

### External Dependencies

- `react-native` - `View`, `Pressable`, `StyleSheet`
- `react-native-reanimated` - height animation for content, rotation animation for chevron (Animated.View, useSharedValue, useAnimatedStyle, withTiming)

### Design System Integration

- Colors come from theme (`useEtoroTheme().colors`):
  - Divider: `dividerSenary` (theme token for subtle separators)
  - Header text: `textPrimaryNeutral` (Figma overlay-neutral-text)
  - Chevron: `textPrimaryNeutral` (normal) or `textDisabledPrimaryNeutral` (disabled)
- Spacing:
  - Container: 20px vertical (X5), 28px horizontal (X7)
  - AccordionItem: `paddingTop: X5` (20px) — top spacing per item; see `accordion-item.tsx` styles.container
  - AccordionHeader: dynamic `marginBottom` only — X1 (4px) when expanded, X5 (20px) when collapsed; no paddingVertical; see `accordion-header.tsx`
  - Content: `paddingBottom: X6` (24px), `paddingRight: X4` (16px)
- Icon size: chevron uses `sm` size
- Animation duration: 300ms for both height and rotation

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Context Architecture

The accordion uses a two-level context pattern:

1. **AccordionContext** - Wraps the entire accordion, provides:
   - `expandedIds` - array of currently expanded item IDs
   - `toggleItem` - function to toggle an item's expanded state
   - `allowMultiple` - whether multiple items can be expanded

2. **AccordionItemContext** - Wraps each item, provides:
   - `id` - unique identifier for this item
   - `isExpanded` - whether this item is currently expanded
   - `disabled` - whether this item is disabled
   - `toggle` - function to toggle this item

**File structure:**

```
context/
├── accordion-context.tsx       # AccordionContext + useAccordionContext hook
├── accordion-item-context.tsx  # AccordionItemContext + useAccordionItemContext hook
└── index.ts                    # exports
```

### Controlled vs Uncontrolled State

The accordion supports two state management patterns:

1. **Uncontrolled** (default): Use `defaultExpandedIds` for initial state
   - Component manages state internally
   - Use `onExpandedChange` to react to changes if needed
   - Simpler for basic use cases

2. **Controlled**: Use `expandedIds` + `onExpandedChange`
   - Parent manages state externally
   - Full control over which items are expanded
   - Useful for complex state logic or persisting state

### Single vs Multiple Expansion

The `allowMultiple` prop controls expansion behavior:

- **Single expansion** (`allowMultiple={false}`, default):
  - Clicking a collapsed item expands it and collapses any previously expanded item
  - Only one item can be expanded at a time

- **Multiple expansion** (`allowMultiple={true}`):
  - Each item toggles independently
  - Multiple items can be expanded simultaneously

### Animation Behavior

The accordion has two animations:

1. **Chevron rotation**:
   - Rotates from 0° (collapsed) to 180° (expanded)
   - Duration: 300ms with timing animation
   - Handled by `useAccordionAnimation` hook

2. **Content height**:
   - Animates from 0 to measured content height
   - Duration: 300ms with timing animation
   - Uses absolute positioning for proper layout during animation
   - First render measures content height, subsequent renders animate

### Accessibility

The accordion includes built-in accessibility support:

- `EtAccordion.Header`:
  - `accessibilityRole="button"` - announces as button to screen readers
  - `accessibilityState={{ expanded, disabled }}` - communicates expansion and disabled state
  - `accessibilityLabel` - uses children text if string

### Visual States

Each item has visual feedback:

- **Normal**: Full opacity, clickable
- **Pressed**: Reduced opacity (0.7) on touch
- **Disabled**: Reduced opacity (0.5), not clickable, chevron uses disabled color
- **Expanded**: Chevron rotated 180°, content visible

### Dividers

Each `EtAccordion.Item` renders a divider below it using `dividerSenary` (theme token). This is built-in and cannot be disabled.

